WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.860
- [Reporter] This is what
Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:04.448
unleashed on Ukraine.

00:00:04.448 --> 00:00:05.281
(booming sound)

00:00:05.281 --> 00:00:06.780
- [Narrator] This is how
some news organizations

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.710
in the US have been covering
Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.600
- [Reporter] Russia's full-scale invasion.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.730
- Russian invasion.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.623
- [Reporter] Russia attacking
Ukraine's fuel deposits.

00:00:15.623 --> 00:00:17.380
- [Narrator] And this
is how it's described

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.201
on Russian state television.

00:00:19.201 --> 00:00:23.201
(reporters in foreign language)

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.220
- The two sides,

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.720
they really have wildly
different descriptions

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.090
of what's going on

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.653
because the Kremlin is really
conscious of public opinion.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.450
- [Narrator] State broadcasters
have been reinforcing

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.610
Russian President
Vladimir Putin's narrative

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.870
that Ukraine and its
Western allies pose threats

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.457
to his country.

00:00:41.457 --> 00:00:46.028
(reporter speaking in foreign language)

00:00:46.028 --> 00:00:47.830
(booming sound)

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.770
- [Narrator] With ongoing
global coverage of the war

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:52.470
and a deluge of information
on social media,

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:53.670
Russian state media outlets

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.310
are using maps and dismissing
Western media reports

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:57.750
to send its own message

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.950
about the invasion of
its nextdoor neighbor.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.040
To understand why Putin decided to attack,

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.010
you first need to know

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:08.189
how he sees Ukraine's
relationship to Russia.

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:12.856
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:14.810
- [Narrator] So the state media

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:17.530
has been giving its
viewers a geography lesson.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.630
This is a map of Ukraine today,

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:20.870
which was a Soviet state

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.960
before it gained its independence in 1991.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:27.130
Here parts of the country
are broken up into sections.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.930
The reporter says that these areas

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:30.940
aren't really Ukraine's but were gifts

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.230
from past Russian and Soviet leaders.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.860
And this yellow part in the middle

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.140
is the only section that's
labeled as Ukrainian territory.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.230
- Maps like these,

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:42.120
the idea is to really shape public opinion

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.080
and give this kind of historical backing

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.640
for their current operation in Ukraine.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:50.990
- [Narrator] And this historical context

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:53.620
was reiterated in Putin's
nearly hour-long speech,

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.663
days before the invasion.

00:01:55.663 --> 00:02:00.663
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.350
- Putin seems to have
been focused on history

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.330
when it comes to Ukraine,

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.830
and he has always mentioned Ukraine

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.650
where it has been part of Russia,

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.313
and it should continue
to be part of Russia.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.660
- [Narrator] Back in 1991,

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.240
Ukrainians held a referendum

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.320
that overwhelmingly supported independence

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.830
from the Soviet Union.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.140
And this decision was backed by Russia.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.440
And as a sovereign state,

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.220
several years later,
Ukraine asked to join NATO.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.300
But Putin objected

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.660
because this would bring
the military alliance closer

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.090
to Russia's doorstep,

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:33.980
a concern that his predecessors shared

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.690
after the break up of the Soviet Union.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.060
So he demanded that the
alliance guarantee Ukraine

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.610
would not get membership.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:41.737
And when there were none.

00:02:41.737 --> 00:02:46.404
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.410
- [Narrator] The state media
has amplified this narrative

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:53.100
that the conflict with
Ukraine isn't Russia's fault,

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.096
but the US and its Western
allies are to blame.

00:02:56.096 --> 00:03:00.846
(reporters speaking in foreign language)

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.160
- [Narrator] A few days
after the invasion,

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.915
Putin raised the stakes again.

00:03:05.915 --> 00:03:10.582
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.310
- [Narrator] He ordered the
country's nuclear forces

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.360
to be put on alert

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.630
as the US and its allies
stepped up pressure

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.240
with new sanctions.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:25.670
(reporter speaking in foreign language)

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.275
- [Narrator] And Russian state
media echoed his message.

00:03:28.275 --> 00:03:32.480
(reporter speaking in foreign language)

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.490
- [Narrator] State media programs

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:36.210
are also running disinformation segments.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.760
This newscast shows what it claims

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.410
to be a tweet from CNN
about an American who died

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.310
during the invasion of Ukraine.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.030
No American causalities have
been reported during the war

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.090
and the Twitter account was suspended.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.950
CNN said the tweet was fabricated

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.470
and the account not affiliated
with the news organization

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:52.690
in any way.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:55.100
The Russian state media
channel, Russia-24,

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.870
didn't respond to a request for comment.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:58.730
Russian state media

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.690
have also repeated the Kremlin's position

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.940
that there are no threats to civilians

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:06.069
and that it's only targeting
military installations.

00:04:06.069 --> 00:04:10.736
(reporter speaking in foreign language)

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.460
- [Narrator] In the first week of war,

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:16.830
Ukrainian officials said the
invasion's civilian death toll

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.780
had reached 2,000.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.640
- These outlets, they're
propagating the Kremlin line

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:23.680
that this is a limited operation

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.530
and also saying that Russia
needs to demilitarize Ukraine.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.490
They're really saving the population

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:30.380
in eastern Ukraine.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.850
The Kremlin wants that
the domestic audience

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.833
sees Russia not as an aggressor.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:36.590
- [Narrator] Before the invasion,

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:39.540
many Russians agreed with
the Kremlin line on Ukraine.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.780
About 60% of those surveyed in Russia

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.950
say tensions in Ukraine

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.660
are the fault of the US and NATO

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:47.328
according to a Russian
independent pollster.

00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:50.310
(crowd speaking in foreign language)

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.490
- [Narrator] But the Kremlin's narrative

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.453
isn't getting to everyone in Russia.

00:04:53.453 --> 00:04:55.050
(crowd speaking in foreign language)

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:55.890
Across the country,

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:59.360
people have been protesting
Putin's decision to invade.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.410
So to continue shaping public opinion,

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.180
the country's communications regulator

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:06.000
ordered all media outlets,
including independent ones,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.400
to only use official government sources.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.340
The government watchdog

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:11.430
and state media
organizations didn't respond

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.180
to a request for comment.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.120
And as the West has
started to cut off Russia

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.990
from the global financial system,

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.540
ordinary citizens are
starting to feel the pain,

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:20.670
lining up at ATMs

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:24.084
to pull out cash as the
Russian currency has plummeted.

00:05:24.084 --> 00:05:28.584
(Dennis speaking in foreign language)

00:05:38.808 --> 00:05:39.641
- [Narrator] And this could provide

00:05:39.641 --> 00:05:41.140
the Kremlin another opportunity

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.240
to cast the US and its allies

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:46.297
as Russia's aggressors as
the war in Ukraine continues.

00:05:46.297 --> 00:05:48.992
(dramatic music)

